      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اضبنهُ</span></b>  <i>He put it in his</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضِبْن</span>, (S, K, TA,) or
<i>on his</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضِبْن</span>; (TA;) or <i>he took it beneath his</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضِبْن</span>, i. e. <i>his</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حِضْن</span> [or <i>the part between his armpit and flank</i>]: (A'Obeyd, TA:) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اضطبنهُ</span></b> 
signifies the same. (S, K, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <i>He straitened him,</i> or <i>it,</i> (K, TA,) <i>by putting him,</i> or <i>it,
beneath his side.</i> (TA.)

